add('Economy','01 · External accounts','Q1 current-account deficit: retain statistical vintages','The September release covered April–June 2025.','The deficit was USD 2.4 billion, 0.2% of GDP.|Goods and services balances moved differently.|The review reports a revised Q4 FY2024–25 surplus of USD 13.4 billion.', 'The current account includes goods, services, income and transfers; it differs from financial flows.','Compare like quarters and underlying flows, not a Q4 surplus mechanically against a Q1 deficit.|June’s initial USD 13.5 billion Q4 estimate must keep its release vintage rather than silently overwrite the later figure.','Release month, reference quarter and revised vintage differ; one quarter does not establish the full-year balance.','How should the quality of external resilience be assessed?')
add('Economy','02 · GST & federalism','GST rationalisation: two main slabs, not only two rates','The 56th Council recommended restructuring.','The main slabs are 5% and 18%.|A special 40% demerit rate covers selected items.|Most changes start 22 September, with specified tobacco/pan-masala categories deferred.','Council recommendations, operative notifications and product classifications are different legal layers.','Simplification can reduce friction while affecting state revenue and credit chains.|Price pass-through depends on competition and input costs, not merely the statutory cut.','Do not say every product has only 5%/18%, or all tobacco rates changed on 22 September.','How can GST simplicity balance compliance, revenue and distribution?',src=['E6-GST','E6-PRS09'],day=22)
add('Economy','03 · Insurance & input credit','Insurance GST relief: exemption differs from zero-rating','Individual-policy relief was recommended.','The announcement covers individual life policies.|Individual health includes family-floater and senior-citizen cover.|Specified reinsurance is included; input-credit treatment still matters.','Exempt output can retain embedded input costs; zero rating is a different tax concept.','Compare actual premiums and coverage, not assume an identical percentage fall for every policy.|AP inclusion needs affordable benefits and accessible claims as well as tax relief.','Do not generalise individual-policy relief to every group policy or assume exemption preserves every input credit.','What converts insurance tax relief into effective protection?',True,src=['E6-GST','E6-PRS09'])
add('Economy','04 · Listing & minority rights','SEBI listing changes: public float and RPTs','The Board approved changes to listing-related requirements.','MPO concerns the initial public offer.|MPS concerns ongoing public shareholding.|RPT changes address materiality, information and omnibus approvals.','An omnibus approval covers defined repetitive transactions, not unlimited immunity from conflict rules.','Flexibility can improve large-issuer access if liquidity and minority safeguards remain credible.|Check final implementation instruments before treating every Board decision as immediately operative.','Do not confuse public float with the retail-investor quota or give every issuer the longest timeline.','How should listing reform balance market access and minority protection?',priority='P2')
add('Economy','05 · Foreign-investor access','SWAGAT-FI: trusted categories, not universal exemption','SEBI approved a unified registration framework.','Eligible categories include central banks and sovereign funds.|The objective is reduced repeated registration across routes.|Full implementation was planned within six months.','Simpler registration does not abolish beneficial-ownership checks or all investment limits.','Risk differentiation can reduce friction if eligibility remains defensible.|Measure actual processing improvements separately from approval.','Do not extend the route automatically to every foreign retail investor or claim rollout was complete immediately.','When is differentiated financial compliance justified?',priority='P2')
add('Polity & Governance','01 · Interim constitutional review','Waqf interim order: targeted restraints, not total stay','The Court declined a complete stay while intervening selectively.','The five-year practice condition was restrained pending a mechanism.|Government-property inquiry consequences received targeted relief.|Council/Board membership caps and a CEO recommendation have different effects.','Interim protection differs from final invalidation; judicial recommendations and mandatory directions differ.','Follow January scrutiny, April enactment and July rules into September litigation.|Read the operative order and subsequent developments for current application.','Do not say the whole Act was stayed, finally upheld, or all membership rules wholly suspended.','How does interim review prevent harm while preserving constitutional adjudication?')
add('Polity & Governance','02 · Electoral inclusion','Bihar SIR: Aadhaar proves identity, not citizenship','The Court directed acceptance for identification in roll revision.','The direction concerned Bihar’s Special Intensive Revision.|Document authenticity could still be checked.|Identity evidence does not settle all voting qualifications.','Citizenship, identity and inclusion in a particular electoral roll are distinct legal questions.','Accessible documents reduce exclusion only when verification and appeals are fair.|A Bihar-specific order is not proof of an identical process in every state.','Do not call Aadhaar proof of Indian citizenship or an unconditional voting entitlement.','How should roll accuracy be reconciled with inclusion and due process?')
add('Society & Welfare','01 · Occupational safety','OSH draft rules: sector-specific welfare duties','Seven rule sets were released for consultation.','They cover sectors including docks, mines, construction and factories.|Employer duties include safety and welfare facilities.|Water, first aid, childcare and exposure protection are themes.','A parent Code, draft rules, commencement and enforcement capacity are separate layers.','Sectoral hazards need worker participation and functioning inspections.|AP construction/industrial workers need actual access, not facilities existing only on paper.','Consultation is not proof every proposed obligation was already operative in September.','How can occupational safety shift towards prevention?',True)
add('Science & Technology','01 · Civilian drones','Draft Drone Bill: airspace, competence and liability','The aviation ministry sought public feedback.','The draft proposes UAS registration and safety requirements.|Pilot competence and third-party insurance are addressed.|Red/yellow/green airspace zones have distinct permission treatment.','Ownership, airspace permission and operator training address different risks.','Proportionate rules can enable agriculture/logistics without ignoring privacy and aviation safety.|AP applications need lawful operation and validated economics, not just demonstrations.','Draft green-zone treatment is not blanket exemption from all safety duties or enacted replacement law.','How should drone regulation balance innovation and accountability?',True)
add('Economy','06 · Maritime finance','Shipbuilding package: finance plus industrial capability','The Cabinet approved a multi-part package.','Financial assistance was extended to March 2036.|The ₹25,000 crore Maritime Development Fund has investment/interest-support components.|A separate development scheme supports clusters.','Gross tonnage capacity, ships delivered and jobs created are different measures.','Patient finance also needs design skills, suppliers, orders and credible contracts.|AP shipyard opportunities depend on viable project-level milestones.','Do not treat investment/job expectations as achieved outcomes or double-count fund components.','What complements finance in a competitive shipbuilding ecosystem?',True)
add('Security','01 · Telecom identity','Draft user-identification rules: biometrics and alternatives','DoT consulted on an identification framework.','Aadhaar authentication has an alternative digital-KYC route in specified cases.|Biometric verification and sharing are proposed.|Replacement, portability and transfer have re-verification conditions.','Identity collection creates retention, access and security risks as well as fraud-control benefits.','Purpose limitation and accessible corrections should accompany stronger checks.|Authentication failure alone does not establish fraud.','Do not label a draft final law or say there is no alternative to Aadhaar authentication.','How can telecom fraud controls avoid exclusion and disproportionate surveillance?')
add('Security','02 · Interception & jurisdiction','Interception amendment: a cross-state request channel','Notified changes modify the 2024 procedures.','Union Home Secretary may issue an order requested beyond a state’s territorial jurisdiction.|The state home secretary makes the specified request.|Agencies designate one or more nodal officers.','Competent authority, lawful grounds, procedure and review must be read together.','Coordination should preserve necessary and proportionate use with accountable records.|Interception and routine KYC serve different purposes.','Do not infer that any officer gained unlimited national interception authority.','What makes interception accountable in a federal system?')
add('Environment','01 · Geothermal energy','Geothermal policy: heat uses as well as electricity','MNRE notified a national framework.','It covers generation and direct heating/cooling uses.|Abandoned wells and industry partnerships are potential routes.|State nodal agencies and exploration support are envisaged.','Geothermal uses subsurface heat and need not generate electricity in every application.','Drilling risk, fluid chemistry and ecology shape viability.|Finance/tax avenues to explore are not automatically adopted concessions.','Policy notification does not establish commissioned plants or universal subsidy entitlement.','How can policy share geothermal exploration risk responsibly?')
add('Environment','02 · Storage rules progression','Storage amendment: consumers added to eligible entities','Rules progressed beyond June’s draft stage.','End consumers may develop, own, lease or operate ESS.|Storage services can be sold beyond utilities/load-despatch centres.|Other applicable technical permissions remain relevant.','Storage shifts electricity across time; it is not a primary energy source or necessarily renewable-fed.','Wider participation helps flexibility with clear pricing and grid obligations.|Compare final text with June’s draft rather than assume every proposal survived.','Do not infer a free battery entitlement or exemption from connectivity and safety requirements.','How can wider storage participation improve reliability?',True)
add('Society & Welfare','02 · Statistical autonomy','Draft ISI Bill: governance and academic accountability','MoSPI sought comments on replacement legislation.','The draft changes statutory governance.|Appointments, board powers and terms are revised.|Institutional funds/corpus are part of the design.','Public finance and professional statistical independence require distinct accountability arrangements.','Assess transparent appointments, academic quality and autonomy safeguards.|A new board alone does not establish better research.','Consultation is not an already replaced Act or proof appointments occurred.','How should research institutions reconcile autonomy with accountability?',priority='P2')
add('Society & Welfare','03 · Medical education','Medical seats: approval is not functioning intake','The Cabinet approved UG/PG expansion support.','Targets are 5,023 UG and 5,000 PG seats by 2028–29.|The four-year outlay is about ₹15,035 crore.|Centre/state support complements institutional upgrades.','Approved seats, permitted intake, enrolled trainees and practising doctors are different stages.','Faculty, clinical exposure and deployment determine access benefits.|AP institutions require specific permissions, not an assumed equal share.','Future targets are not all operational September admissions.','How can seat expansion improve healthcare rather than counts alone?',True)
add('Society & Welfare','04 · Early-childhood convergence','Anganwadi–school co-location: two models','Joint guidelines seek continuity into primary education.','One model physically co-locates centres and schools.|Another maps a centre to a nearby grade-one school.|Child records and curricula require alignment.','Co-location does not erase nutrition, care or early-childhood developmental duties.','Shared facilities help with age-appropriate pedagogy and adequate staff.|AP access for younger children/mothers should not worsen through relocation.','Do not say every centre must move physically or schooling replaces all ICDS functions.','How can convergence strengthen continuity without weakening child care?',True)
add('Economy','07 · Circular minerals','Critical-mineral recycling scheme: recovery beyond collection','The Cabinet approved a mission-linked incentive scheme.','The ₹1,500 crore scheme runs FY2025–26 to FY2030–31.|Feedstocks include e-waste and lithium-ion battery scrap.|Capital/operational support has caps and milestones.','Collection, dismantling, recovery and refining are different value-chain steps.','Safe processing and demand for recovered materials determine benefits.|Connect mission, metal EPR and mining changes without conflating their legal roles.','Do not infer grants for unregistered handlers or instant mineral self-sufficiency.','How can recycling incentives build safe domestic recovery?')
add('International Relations','01 · Investment protection','India–Israel investment agreement signed','A bilateral investment framework was signed.','The review notes protection against expropriation.|Transfer and dispute-resolution provisions feature.|Investment safeguards differ from tariff concessions.','An investment agreement and a goods FTA are distinct instruments.','Predictability should coexist with legitimate public regulation.|Signature does not prove entry into force or realised investment.','Do not describe this as a completed goods FTA or insurance against all commercial loss.','How should investment protection preserve policy space?',priority='P2')
add('International Relations','02 · Standards recognition','Australia organic MRA: product scope matters','The arrangement recognises specified certification systems.','It sits under ECTA.|Coverage includes specified plant products, processed plant foods and wine.|Exclusions limit eligible products.','Mutual recognition reduces repeated certification, not all food-safety/import duties.','Traceability and applicable schedules determine exporter benefits.|AP producers must check product coverage rather than assume animal/fish products qualify.','Do not equate recognition with universal zero tariffs or every organic-labelled product.','How can standards cooperation improve credible market access?',True,priority='P2')
add('Polity & Governance','03 · Electoral ethics','Criminalisation: allegations differ from conviction','The magazine reviewed ADR affidavit analysis.','Affidavits disclose declared cases.|Pending cases and convictions have different legal status.|Party selection, disclosure and trial delays affect accountability.','Integrity objectives do not make every accused person guilty or every prosecution politically neutral.','Fair timely trials and transparent party decisions complement voter information.|Connect August custody proposals without claiming enactment.','Do not label case percentages as convicted-minister percentages or quote undated denominators.','How can integrity reform resist both criminal influence and malicious prosecution?',slug='criminalisation-of-politics')
add('Polity & Governance','04 · Judicial capacity','Judicial pendency: stocks, flows and unequal delay','The issue revisited case backlogs.','Pendency is a dated stock.|Institution/disposal and case-age profiles measure different things.|Staffing, procedure, legal aid and infrastructure affect delay.','A disposal ratio does not prove old cases declined or fair access improved.','Prioritise vulnerable litigants and improve government litigation practices.|Avoid unverified budget/litigant-share claims or permanently fixed NJDG totals.','Do not treat an undated count as current or speed as a substitute for due process.','How should judicial performance be judged beyond disposals?',slug='judicial-pendency')
add('Science & Technology','02 · Biomanufacturing','Biofoundry Network: August launch, September coverage','The network launched on 25 August was reviewed in September.','BioE3 links biotechnology with economy, environment and employment.|Biofoundries use automated design–build–test workflows.|Shared facilities support translation beyond proof of concept.','Laboratory feasibility, manufacturing scale and commercial demand are different tests.','Infrastructure needs biosafety, quality, trained staff and usable access rules.|Do not call BioE3 India’s first-ever biotechnology policy.','Coverage month is not launch date; a network announcement does not prove commercial success.','What helps biotechnology cross the scale-up gap?',slug='national-biofoundry-network-bioe3-policy')
add('Environment','03 · EIA participation','Consultation exemption is not exemption from all appraisal','The issue discussed specified strategic-mineral projects.','Consultation collects local concerns/written responses.|The described exemption is category-specific.|Central appraisal remains a separate requirement.','EIA stages, forest/community rights and other permissions are distinct legal obligations.','Strategic security should not erase local ecological evidence.|AP mineral/coastal projects require exact project-specific legal checks.','Do not call strategic status an automatic waiver of all environmental/community duties.','How can strategic-resource policy retain credible environmental accountability?',True,slug='public-consultation-and-environmental-impact-assessment-eia')
add('Environment','04 · Risk financing','Disaster finance: exposure is not just population','Hill-state concerns prompted risk-index debate.','Risk combines hazard, exposure and vulnerability.|Relief and mitigation finance have different roles.|Composite indices need transparent indicators.','An index is an allocation tool, not a physical prediction of all future losses.','Hill and AP coastal risks differ, but both need local vulnerability evidence.|Transfers should encourage mitigation rather than poor reporting.','A request to revise an index is not an adopted Finance Commission formula.','How can transfers reflect vulnerability while rewarding prevention?',True,slug='disaster-risk-financing')
add('International Relations','03 · Nepal transition','Nepal protests and interim leadership','The issue examined September’s transition.','Grievances involved corruption and social-media restrictions.|Sushila Karki became interim Prime Minister.|Interim arrangements differ from later electoral outcomes.','Digital mobilisation does not automatically represent every citizen or resolve constitutional continuity.','Neighbourhood policy should respect sovereignty and practical people-to-people ties.|Election plans must not be presented as elections already held.','Do not call a transition announcement a completed permanent constitutional settlement.','How can protest legitimacy translate into durable democratic institutions?',slug='gen-z-protest-in-nepal')
add('Society & Welfare','05 · Domestic violence','PWDVA at twenty: remedies beyond physical injury','The issue revisited the 2005 Act.','Abuse includes physical, sexual, emotional/verbal and economic forms.|Residence, protection and monetary orders address different needs.|Protection officers/providers support access.','Residence protection is not automatically a transfer of ownership; case-specific scope matters.','Rights require safe reporting, shelter and enforceable orders.|A statutory endeavour/timeframe is not a guarantee every case ends within 60 days.','Enactment and commencement anniversaries differ; an allegation does not automatically establish every legal element.','What closes the gap between remedies and real safety?',True,slug='protection-of-women-from-domestic-violence-act-pwdva-2005')
add('Culture & History','01 · Economic nationalism','Naoroji bicentenary: the drain theory linkage','The issue marked 200 years since his 1825 birth.','He analysed colonial resource drain.|He presided over Congress in 1886, 1893 and 1906.|His work includes Poverty and Un-British Rule in India.','The drain critique concerned colonial political/fiscal relations, not every modern international payment.','Connect economic nationalism with critical use of fiscal evidence.|He was a Welby Commission member, not its chairman.','Do not equate the drain theory with every current-account deficit or misattribute commission chairmanship.','How did economic critique strengthen Indian nationalism?',slug='200th-birth-anniversary-of-dadabhai-naoroji-1',priority='P2')
add('Culture & History','02 · Social reform','Self-Respect Movement centenary: dignity and rationalism','Periyar’s movement began in 1925.','It challenged caste hierarchy.|It promoted rationalism and women’s equality.|Self-respect marriages questioned ritual monopoly.','Social practice and subsequent statutory marriage recognition are separate historical stages.','Compare reform traditions without assuming identical ideologies across phases.|Do not backdate later legislative recognition to the movement’s launch.','The centenary does not mean equality was fully achieved or all later law began in 1925.','How did self-respect politics link personal dignity and structural reform?',slug='100-years-of-the-self-respect-movement-in-tamil-nadu',priority='P2')
add('Society & Welfare','06 · GS4 integrity','Moral integrity: consistency under conflicting pressures','Judicial remarks prompted the issue’s ethics discussion.','Integrity concerns values and conduct.|Honesty/impartiality face organisational and personal pressures.|Public decisions need scrutinizable reasons.','Lawfulness may not exhaust ethical responsibility, but personal conviction cannot override constitutional duty.','Use disclosure, recusal, reasons and fair procedure as safeguards.|Case answers should identify stakeholders/options/consequences rather than repeat quotations alone.','Loyalty to a superior is not automatically integrity; good intentions do not cure discrimination.','How should an official act when pressure conflicts with impartial duty?',slug='moral-integrity',priority='P2')
add('Andhra Pradesh','01 · Health finance','AP hybrid health approval: procurement before active cover','The 4 September Cabinet decision was reported the next day.','The proposal integrates AB-PMJAY and Dr NTR Vaidya Seva.|Insurance/trust roles and an RFP process were discussed.|Secondary summaries conflict on category-wise coverage caps.','Approval, procurement, issuance, hospital access and settled claims are separate milestones.','Use the operative GO/RFP/policy for entitlements, exclusions and provider payments.|Do not promise a uniform ₹25 lakh to every household from conflicting secondary accounts.','A Cabinet headline does not prove every citizen already had active insurance.','How should hybrid health finance be evaluated for reliable equitable protection?',True,src=['E6-APHEALTH'],day=4)
add('Andhra Pradesh','02 · Medical PPP','AP medical-college PPPs: contracts determine public value','The same Cabinet meeting approved a PPP route for ten colleges.','Private participation concerns development/operations under contracts.|Procurement and regulatory approvals remain necessary.|Education access and hospital services need separate safeguards.','A PPP allocates contractual risks; it is not automatically proof of outright sale or universally free service.','Assess fees, seat allocation, faculty and enforceable service obligations.|National expansion support does not certify each state institution’s readiness.','Ten approved projects are not ten fully staffed colleges already admitting students.','What protects public value in medical-education PPPs?',True,src=['E6-APHEALTH'],day=4)
