add('Economy','01 · Monetary policy','October MPC: hold with a neutral stance','The policy review retained the repo rate.','Repo remained 5.5%.|The stance remained neutral.|FY2025–26 growth was projected at 6.8%.','The policy rate, stance and forecast are distinct signals.','A neutral stance permits data-dependent choices, not a promise of the next move.|Forecasts depend on assumptions and are not measured annual growth.','Do not confuse the projection with an NSO outturn or neutral with a permanent rate freeze.','How should monetary policy weigh inflation and growth?')
add('Economy','02 · Inflation measurement','Q2 CPI: falling food prices, not general deflation','Quarterly inflation moderated.','Average CPI inflation was 1.7%.|Food inflation averaged −1.6%.|These are quarterly aggregates, not identical monthly or household experiences.','Disinflation is slower positive inflation; deflation is a falling price index.','Food volatility can lower headline inflation without eliminating other pressures.|Compare the same period and basket before drawing welfare conclusions.','Negative food inflation does not establish negative overall CPI or lower prices for every household.','What limits headline CPI as a measure of lived inflation?')
add('Polity & Governance','01 · Pay commission','Eighth Pay Commission: terms, not a pay award','The Cabinet approved Terms of Reference.','The commission examines central-government pay/pension matters.|Recommendations and government acceptance are separate stages.|Terms of Reference are not notified revised salaries.','A commission recommends; expenditure requires accepted decisions and implementation instruments.','Assess fiscal space and service quality as well as consumption effects.|No fitment factor should be invented from speculative headlines.','Approval is not proof salaries already rose or that a guessed factor is official.','How can public-pay reform balance fairness and fiscal sustainability?')
add('Economy','03 · Deposit protection','Risk-based deposit-insurance premium: draft approach','RBI consulted on differentiated premiums.','The proposal links bank risk to premium treatment.|Deposit insurance protects eligible deposits subject to law.|Premium design and depositor coverage are different questions.','Deposit insurance is not protection against every investment loss or unlimited bank liabilities.','Risk pricing can reduce cross-subsidy but needs credible metrics and transition safeguards.|Do not infer a changed coverage ceiling from a premium consultation.','Draft premium reform does not automatically expand every depositor’s insured amount.','How can deposit protection preserve confidence without weakening discipline?')
add('Economy','04 · Cross-border finance','Rupee lending to neighbours: permitted scope matters','RBI eased specified cross-border lending rules.','The reviewed countries are Nepal, Bhutan and Sri Lanka.|Authorised lender and transaction conditions still apply.|Permission is not an automatic loan to every applicant.','Currency denomination, borrower eligibility and repayment risk are distinct.','Rupee finance can support regional links without guaranteeing currency-risk elimination.|Keep notified permission separate from actual disbursement.','Do not expand the measure to every country or describe loans as grants.','How can regional rupee finance balance integration and prudence?',priority='P2')
add('Economy','05 · Capital-market consultation','Capital-market exposure and ECB reforms: proposals','RBI released draft changes.','Capital-market exposure rules concern bank risk limits.|External commercial borrowing has a separate regulatory framework.|Consultation is not final implementation.','Bank exposure, foreign borrowing and equity flows are different channels.','Simplification needs safeguards against concentrated and currency-mismatched risk.|Read final directions before applying proposed limits to transactions.','A proposal is not an already effective permission; do not mix domestic bank limits and ECB conditions.','What makes financial liberalisation prudentially credible?',priority='P2')
add('Economy','06 · Retirement and fund rules','NPS and mutual funds: distinguish consultations','Regulators considered changes to investment frameworks.','NPS investment proposals concern retirement savings.|Mutual-fund proposals concern a separate product framework.|Final rules and individual product mandates still matter.','An investment ceiling is not a guaranteed return or a compulsory allocation.','Long horizons do not remove market, governance or liquidity risks.|Historical review notes should not substitute for current scheme documents.','Do not merge draft NPS and mutual-fund rules or promise returns from a wider investment universe.','How should pension flexibility protect retirement security?',priority='P2')
add('Economy','07 · Electricity reform','Draft Electricity Amendment: distribution and public duties','The ministry consulted on proposed statutory changes.','Distribution reform features in the draft.|Tariffs, cost recovery and subsidy arrangements require separate scrutiny.|Draft legislation is not an enacted replacement.','A subsidy promise, budgeted transfer and utility receipt are different financial stages.','Efficiency and contestability need universal-service and consumer safeguards.|AP analysis should examine farm support, utility finances and actual state implementation.','Do not claim draft provisions already changed every consumer tariff.','How can distribution reform reconcile viability and universal access?',True)
add('Agriculture','01 · Pulses mission','Pulses self-reliance: production and procurement linkages','The Cabinet approved the mission.','The outlay is ₹11,440 crore.|The period is FY2025–26 to FY2030–31.|Seed, productivity and procurement linkages support domestic supply.','Self-reliance is an objective; output, imports and farmer income need separate evidence.','Assured demand helps only with operational procurement, quality acceptance and payment.|AP crop choices also depend on water, local prices and agronomy.','An approved mission does not prove imports ended or every farmer received a universal cash amount.','What makes pulses diversification viable for farmers?',True)
add('Agriculture','02 · Price support','Rabi MSP: marketing year and actual purchase differ','The Cabinet announced MSPs for the coming marketing season.','Wheat MSP is ₹2,585 per quintal.|Gram is ₹5,875 and masur ₹7,000 per quintal.|These are administered support prices, not guaranteed realised market prices everywhere.','MSP announcement, procurement eligibility and actual purchase are separate.','Market access and effective procurement determine benefits beyond headline increases.|A quintal is 100 kg; use the notified crop and season.','Do not quote these as per-kilogram prices or assured payments to every grower.','How can price support improve income without distorting resource use?',True)
add('Agriculture','03 · Fertiliser support','Rabi P&K subsidy: nutrient support, not direct cash','The Cabinet approved seasonal nutrient-based support.','The approved requirement is ₹37,952 crore.|The measure concerns phosphatic and potassic fertilisers.|Subsidy parameters differ from farmers’ final retail bills.','Nutrient-based subsidy is distinct from a uniform transfer to every cultivator.','Balanced nutrition, availability and soil information matter with affordability.|Keep urea’s separate policy treatment distinct.','Do not divide the outlay into a promised individual payment or claim it covers all fertilisers identically.','How can fertiliser support encourage balanced use?',True)
add('Society & Welfare','01 · Consultation versus commencement','Labour and sports drafts: track legal stages','The month’s policy review records consultation proposals.','Draft subordinate rules differ from parent enactments.|Institutional proposals need notification and operational capacity.|Submission deadlines are not commencement dates.','Law-making, delegated rules and enforcement are separate parts of implementation.','Read each sector’s final instrument rather than infer automatic operation from a ministry draft.|A sports governance proposal is not proof every body is already constituted.','Do not combine unrelated draft rules into a claim that all reforms took effect together.','Why is implementation capacity as important as statutory design?',priority='P2')
add('Security','01 · Takedown accountability','IT takedown procedure: reasons and identified content','Notified amendments changed procedural requirements.','Reasoned orders and identification of URLs/content are relevant safeguards.|Authorised decision-making differs from informal requests.|Synthetic-content labelling was a separate draft.','A takedown order, platform response and court review are different stages.','Traceable reasons support accountability and meaningful challenge.|Content restrictions still require lawful grounds and proportionality.','Do not conflate a notified procedural amendment with a separate AI-labelling consultation.','How can takedown procedures protect both safety and expression?')
add('Science & Technology','01 · Synthetic media','Synthetic-content labelling: draft, not blanket ban','A separate consultation addressed AI-generated content.','The proposal concerns identification/labelling obligations.|Synthetic media includes legitimate as well as harmful uses.|Final text and applicability need separate verification.','Provenance, authenticity and truthfulness are related but different.','Labels need reliability, accessibility and remedies against false attribution.|Do not assume a label alone prevents fraud or an unlabelled item is genuine.','A labelling draft is not an enacted ban on every AI image.','What safeguards make synthetic-media governance effective?')
add('Economy','08 · Mineral value chains','Mining rules: extraction permissions and safeguards','The review records changes to mineral regulation.','Mining authorisation and environmental clearance remain distinct.|Lease conditions and monitoring affect compliance.|Processing and recycling are different value-chain activities.','Mineral access alone does not establish viable downstream capacity.','Connect critical-mineral incentives with traceability and local safeguards.|Check the precise amended provision before applying it to an AP lease.','Do not infer that a mining-rule amendment waives every forest/environment/community obligation.','How can mineral security preserve accountable resource governance?',True,priority='P2')
add('Economy','09 · Industrial incentives','Specialty-steel PLI: thresholds are not payouts','The review discusses revised eligibility parameters.','Specified investment thresholds include ₹150 crore and ₹50 crore.|Thresholds depend on the relevant category.|Eligibility does not itself establish an incentive disbursement.','Investment commitments, production milestones and verified incentives differ.','Evaluate additional capacity, technology and fiscal cost rather than applications alone.|Use the operative scheme schedule for category-specific figures.','Do not treat a qualifying investment threshold as money paid to every producer.','How should production incentives demonstrate additionality?',priority='P2')
add('Environment','01 · Industrial carbon regulation','GHG intensity targets: relative does not mean absolute','Targets were notified for four industrial sectors.','Compliance uses emissions intensity measures.|Production levels affect total emissions.|Facility applicability and monitoring rules matter.','Absolute emissions equal output multiplied by intensity on a consistent basis.','An intensity reduction can coexist with higher total emissions as output grows.|Credible measurement and verification underpin a functioning compliance market.','Do not call every intensity improvement an equal absolute emissions reduction.','How can intensity targets support credible industrial decarbonisation?')
add('Security','02 · Road safety governance','National Road Safety Board: expertise versus execution','The review records institutional road-safety developments.','A national expert body has a different role from local enforcement.|Engineering, vehicles and emergency response all matter.|Constitution/notification does not prove a measured fall in deaths.','Road safety is a systems problem rather than solely driver blame.','Track outcomes with exposure-aware indicators and reliable reporting.|AP implementation needs road-owner, police and health coordination.','Do not treat a board as replacing every state agency or announcing a proven casualty reduction.','How can institutions turn safety advice into measurable prevention?',True,priority='P2')
add('Polity & Governance','02 · Prisons and undertrials','Prison Statistics 2023: publication year is not data year','The magazine examined the NCRB report.','The reference period is 2023.|Undertrials and convicted prisoners are different legal categories.|Occupancy reflects capacity and inmate counts at a dated point.','Custody is not a finding of guilt; overcrowding also affects health and legal access.','Bail, legal aid, case management and humane facilities need coordinated reform.|A model prison law does not automatically replace every state statute.','Do not label 2023 statistics as 2025 observations or undertrials as convicted offenders.','How should prison reform protect liberty and public safety?',slug='prison-reforms')
add('International Relations','01 · EFTA agreement','TEPA enters into force: targets are not realised flows','The agreement became effective on 1 October.','It was signed in March 2024.|EFTA comprises Iceland, Liechtenstein, Norway and Switzerland.|The USD 100 billion investment objective spans fifteen years.','A trade framework, investment target and measured capital inflow differ.','Assess tariff schedules, origin rules and institutional follow-through.|EFTA is not the European Union.','Do not call the target money already received or date the signature to October 2025.','What determines whether trade agreements deliver investment linkages?',slug='india-european-free-trade-association-efta-trade-and-economic-partnership-agreement-tepa')
add('Economy','10 · Factory statistics','ASI 2023–24: nominal GVA and reference period','The issue reviewed the Annual Survey of Industries.','The reported current-price GVA growth is 11.89%.|The survey reference year is 2023–24.|Registered factory-sector statistics do not equal the entire economy.','Nominal growth includes price effects; real output needs appropriate deflation.','Use employment, productivity and industry composition alongside aggregate GVA.|Publication in 2025 does not turn these into 2025–26 observations.','Do not describe current-price GVA growth as real GDP growth for all sectors.','How should factory data inform industrial policy?',slug='annual-survey-of-industries-asi-for-2023-24')
add('International Relations','02 · Fisheries subsidies','WTO fisheries agreement: September entry, October review','The agreement entered into force on 15 September.','It targets specified harmful fisheries subsidies.|India had not ratified at the reviewed point.|Entry into force and obligations for a particular member differ.','A multilateral agreement does not automatically bind every non-accepting member identically.','Balance sustainability, monitoring and developing-country livelihoods.|Do not treat this text as a complete settlement of every overcapacity negotiation.','October magazine coverage is not the entry date; India’s non-ratification must not be omitted.','How can fisheries rules reconcile sustainability and development?',True,slug='wto-agreement-on-fisheries-subsidies')
add('Security','03 · Cybercrime treaty','UN Cybercrime Convention: signing is not force','The convention opened for signature.','Entry into force requires forty ratifications and the stipulated ninety-day interval.|Signature and ratification are separate acts.|Cooperation must be read with safeguards and domestic law.','Treaty adoption, signature, ratification and entry into force are distinct milestones.','Cross-border evidence cooperation needs necessity, proportionality and rights protection.|Do not imply an opening ceremony alone made all obligations operative.','Do not say the treaty was already in force merely because states signed it.','How should cybercrime cooperation protect privacy and due process?',slug='united-nations-convention-against-cybercrime')
add('Environment','02 · Biosphere geography','Cold Desert: UNESCO’s designated geography','UNESCO’s profile records 2025 designation.','The site is in Himachal Pradesh’s Lahaul–Spiti.|The profile gives 777,000 hectares and elevations of 3,300–6,600 metres.|Pin Valley and Kibber/Chandratal protected areas feature.','A biosphere reserve’s zonation and designated boundary differ from an entire ecological region.','Use the official profile to correct overbroad Ladakh–Kinnaur descriptions.|Recognition does not erase local livelihoods or automatically apply national-park rules everywhere.','Do not relocate the designated reserve to Ladakh or equate a biosphere reserve with a single national park.','How can biosphere governance reconcile conservation and livelihoods?',src=['E6-COLD'],slug='cold-desert-biosphere-reserve')
add('Society & Welfare','02 · Hunger measurement','GHI 2025: composite score, not a UN hunger census','The issue discussed the index and its limitations.','India ranked 102 of 123 with a score of 25.8, classified serious.|Four indicators include undernourishment, child wasting, stunting and mortality.|Inputs have different reference periods.','A composite index and a directly observed headcount are different measures.','Compare methodology and indicator changes, not rank alone.|The index is not co-published by UN agencies merely because inputs use international datasets.','Do not call 25.8 the percentage of all Indians hungry or assume rank changes establish causation.','How should composite indices guide policy without replacing national evidence?',slug='global-hunger-index-1')
add('Culture & History','01 · Social reform linkages','Narayana Guru: dignity, education and organisation','The magazine profiled the reformer.','He lived from 1856 to 1928.|His reform tradition challenged caste exclusion.|Education and social organisation are key analytical linkages.','A historical profile’s publication date does not establish an anniversary claim.','Compare Guru and Self-Respect reform without erasing their different settings.|The claimed 2025 death centenary conflicts with his 1928 death and is not retained.','Do not repeat an unsupported centenary or assume all reform traditions were identical.','How did social reform connect dignity with institutional change?',slug='sree-narayana-guru',priority='P2')
add('Andhra Pradesh','01 · AI infrastructure','Google Vizag AI hub: announced future investment','Google announced its first Indian AI hub on 14 October.','The proposal is about USD 15 billion across 2026–30.|It envisages gigawatt-scale infrastructure and a subsea gateway.|AdaniConneX and Airtel feature in the issuer announcement.','Announced commitments, financial closure, construction and operation are separate milestones.','AP opportunities need reliable power/water, skills and resilient connectivity.|Commissioned economic projections are not observed AP GDP gains or verified job outcomes.','Do not say the entire investment was spent or the hub commissioned in October 2025.','How can AP convert digital investment into sustainable local value?',True,src=['E6-GOOGLE'],day=14)
add('Andhra Pradesh','02 · Coastal risk','Cyclone Montha: observed landfall-start versus forecasts','An IMD-attributed report recorded landfall starting near Kakinada on 28 October.','The account describes a severe cyclonic storm.|The cited bulletin concerns the start of the crossing process.|Final wind, track and loss totals require later authoritative reports.','Forecast intensity, observed conditions and audited impacts are different evidence types.','Connect risk finance with evacuation, warnings and resilient infrastructure.|Do not turn a prior forecast wind range into an observed final maximum.','This source does not certify final damage totals or a completed crossing at its start time.','What makes coastal preparedness effective before, during and after landfall?',True,src=['E6-MONTHA'],day=28)
add('Science & Technology','02 · Nobel physics','Physics Nobel: quantum behaviour in electrical circuits','The official 2025 award recognised macroscopic quantum effects.','Laureates are John Clarke, Michel H. Devoret and John M. Martinis.|The citation concerns macroscopic quantum mechanical tunnelling.|Energy quantisation in an electric circuit is also recognised.','Quantum tunnelling is not classical passage over an energy barrier.','Connect circuit-scale quantum behaviour to technological possibilities without claiming a universal fault-tolerant computer was delivered.|Recognition of foundational work differs from immediate commercial readiness.','Do not swap the laureates with chemistry or claim the award certifies all quantum-computing promises.','Why do foundational experiments matter for emerging technologies?',src=['E6-NOBEL'],priority='P2')
add('Science & Technology','03 · Nobel chemistry','Chemistry Nobel: metal–organic frameworks','The award recognised MOF development.','Laureates are Susumu Kitagawa, Richard Robson and Omar M. Yaghi.|MOFs combine metal-based nodes and organic linkers.|Porous frameworks enable diverse adsorption/separation research.','Porosity and tunable chemistry do not make every material suitable for every gas or operating condition.','Assess stability, cost and regeneration energy before extrapolating a laboratory application.|Applications include gas handling and water-harvesting research, not universal guaranteed deployment.','Do not confuse MOFs with a single metal alloy or claim identical selectivity across all frameworks.','How can porous-material research translate into useful environmental technology?',src=['E6-NOBEL'],priority='P2')
add('Science & Technology','04 · Nobel medicine','Medicine Nobel: peripheral immune tolerance','The award recognised mechanisms of immune restraint.','Laureates are Mary E. Brunkow, Fred Ramsdell and Shimon Sakaguchi.|Peripheral immune tolerance is the official theme.|Regulatory T cells and FOXP3 provide key study connections.','Tolerance helps prevent harmful responses to self; it differs from general absence of immunity.','Immune regulation matters for autoimmunity and treatment design.|Foundational discovery does not mean a universal cure has been approved.','Do not confuse peripheral tolerance with every vaccine mechanism or promise a cure from an award citation.','How does understanding immune regulation inform medicine?',src=['E6-NOBEL'],priority='P2')
add('Awards & Sports','01 · Nobel humanities','Literature and Peace: distinguish the citations','The official aggregate lists the 2025 recipients.','Literature: László Krasznahorkai, for a visionary oeuvre and art’s power amid apocalyptic terror.|Peace: Maria Corina Machado, for democratic rights and peaceful transition in Venezuela.|The awards recognise different fields and institutions.','An award citation is not a judicial verdict on every political dispute.','For Prelims pair recipient, field and country/context; for Mains examine democratic participation and cultural expression.|Avoid substituting a personal political judgment for the actual citation.','Do not interchange the two recipients or call the Peace award a completed political transition.','How can peaceful civic participation strengthen democratic legitimacy?',src=['E6-NOBEL'],priority='P2')
add('Economy','11 · Nobel growth theory','Economic sciences: innovation and creative destruction','The prize recognised explanations of innovation-led growth.','Joel Mokyr was recognised for technological prerequisites of sustained growth.|Philippe Aghion and Peter Howitt were recognised for creative destruction.|Creative destruction links new technologies to displacement of old activities.','Innovation, diffusion, institutions and transition costs differ from a simple increase in spending.','Use skills, competition and social protection to connect growth theory with policy.|A theory does not prove every disruptive firm improves social welfare.','Do not attribute all three laureates to one identical contribution or ignore displaced workers.','How can innovation policy support growth while managing adjustment costs?',src=['E6-NOBEL'],priority='P2')
